E1 — INITIAL LOAD FAILURE AND RECOVERY

Code trace:
  social-store.ts refresh():
    - Sets isLoading=true, error=null
    - Fires Promise.all([connections, feed]) 
    - If connRes.ok → uses data; else pushes error to errors[]
    - If feedRes.ok → uses data; else pushes error to errors[]
    - On success: set({connections, feed, isLoading:false, error: null or partial})
    - On catch: set({isLoading:false, error: message})
    - PARTIAL FAILURE: if one succeeds and other fails, error="Partial failure: feed (500)"
      but the successful data IS set. UI shows error banner + whatever data loaded.

  notification-store.ts refresh():
    - Sets isLoading=true, error=null
    - If !res.ok → throws Error → catch sets isLoading=false, error=message
    - No partial failure path (single request)

  social-screen.tsx FeedPane:
    - loading = isLoading && feed.length === 0 → shows skeleton
    - error banner shown when error && subTab === 'feed'
    - Empty state when feed.length === 0 && !loading
    - No explicit retry button — user must click Refresh or reload

  NotificationBell:
    - isLoading → "Loading..." text
    - No error display in notification list component
    - Error stored in store but NOT rendered in UI

